A('1964-0804-storm', '1964-08-04', VH, 'Gulf of Tonkin. A great storm Aug. 4, the sea black: the Navy\'s 12 torpedo boats are at anchor in their base. The history takes the "Gulf of Tonkin incident" of that day to be an invention of the Americans and cites the cable of the patrol\'s commander, Rear Adm. Herrick, sent that day to the Pentagon, that the torpedo contacts "appear doubtful".', 'III, 365–66', place='gulf-of-tonkin', also=['vietnam'], check='the American record of Aug. 4, not read here, is in the calendar; the history\'s account that no attack took place.')
